[{"id":"a","label":"(a)","prompt":"State which group is more variable in the middle 50%, and justify it.","kind":"text","points":2,"hints":["The IQR measures the middle half of the data.","14 against 9."],"strand":"D(i)","accepted":["students, because their IQR of 14 is larger than the teachers'' 9, so their middle 50% covers a wider range"],"keywords":[["students"],["larger"],["teachers''"],["middle"],["covers"],["wider"]],"minKeywordGroups":4},{"id":"b","label":"(b)","prompt":"Evaluate the governor''s claim about the ranges.","kind":"text","points":2,"hints":["Compare 42 with 55: which range is larger?","The range is sensitive to just two values, the extremes."],"strand":"D(ii)","accepted":["the claim is wrong: the teachers'' range is 55 against the students'' 42, so the teachers'' journeys are more spread at the extremes; the students are only more variable in the middle"],"keywords":[["claim"],["wrong"],["teachers''"],["range"],["against"],["students''"]],"minKeywordGroups":4},{"id":"c","label":"(c)","prompt":"Describe the difference between the groups using the medians.","kind":"text","points":2,"hints":["Compare 31 with 22.","State the difference in minutes and what it means."],"strand":"D(iii)","accepted":["a typical teacher travels about 9 minutes longer than a typical student"],"keywords":[["typical"],["teacher"],["travels"],["minutes"],["longer"],["student"]],"minKeywordGroups":4}],"marking":"(a) 2 marks: 1 for naming students, 1 for citing the IQRs. (b) 2 marks: 1 for correcting the range comparison, 1 for explaining the range''s sensitivity. (c) 2 marks: 1 for the 9-minute difference, 1 for saying what it means.","marking_criteria":"(a) 2 marks: 1 for naming students, 1 for citing the IQRs. (b) 2 marks: 1 for correcting the range comparison, 1 for explaining the range''s sensitivity. (c) 2 marks: 1 for the 9-minute difference, 1 for saying what it means.","response_tools":["rich_text","math"],"response_requirement":"text","response_guidance":"Use the specific numbers in each answer; a comparison without figures earns no marks."},"marking":"(a) 2 marks: 1 for naming students, 1 for citing the IQRs. (b) 2 marks: 1 for correcting the range comparison, 1 for explaining the range''s sensitivity. (c) 2 marks: 1 for the 9-minute difference, 1 for saying what it means."},{"n":30,"t":"assess_parts","p":"A company advertises ''average salaries of $48 000'' for 100 employees. The grouped salary data are:\n\n$10 000–20 000: 42 employees\n$20 000–30 000: 26\n$30 000–40 000: 14\n$40 000–60 000: 12\n$60 000–100 000: 6\n\n(a) Calculate the estimated mean using midpoints.\n(b) Explain why the advertised figure may be misleading and suggest a better measure.\n(c) Describe the distribution''s shape from the table.","d":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A company advertises ''average salaries of "},{"type":"text","text":"$48 000'' for 100 employees. The grouped salary data are:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"$10 000–20 000: 42 employees\n$"},{"type":"text","text":"20 000–30 000: 26\n"},{"type":"text","text":"$30 000–40 000: 14\n$"},{"type":"text","text":"40 000–60 000: 12\n"},{"type":"text","text":"$60 000–100 000: 6"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(a) Calculate the estimated mean using midpoints.\n(b) Explain why the advertised figure may be misleading and suggest a better measure.\n(c) Describe the distribution''s shape from the table."}]}]},"e":"Σf x = $2 850 000 over 100 employees gives an estimated mean of $28 500. Since 82% earn under $30 000, the advertised $48 000 misrepresents a typical salary; the median is more representative. The long right tail makes the distribution positively skewed.","m":9,"df":"hard","tp":"histograms","st":"histograms","cfg":{"source":"myp-mock-myp4-mock","question_number":30,"paper_section":"B","myp_criterion":"D","strand":"D(i)","next_time_hint":"Compare the estimated mean with the advertised claim and 